  "summary": "The path moves coherently from deciding what to teach to deciding what evidence is enough. The preceding7.18 differentiates demonstrations, preferences and sampled-answer feedback. Chapter8 narrows style into observable rules, distinguishes prompts from changed weights, and uses paired questions, effective answer positions and LoRA to show that writing can change while arithmetic remains wrong. Its judge controls keep answer identity separate from display position and information separate from length. Chapter9 carries the same component-wise assessment into missing evidence, factual correction, trusted authorization and quoted-text boundaries; its strong original-template matches are immediately qualified by failed wording changes. Calibration then shows why sharper candidate probabilities cannot repair wrong answers. Chapter10 starts a new input route explicitly, building RGB axes→patch sequence→shared features→positions→projector→expanded targets, while preserving the earlier token/position/loss distinctions. Its separate contrastive branch retrieves one of six known descriptions and is not presented as generated understanding. The next introduction and11.1 return to the generative interface and require correct image-dependent answers, so neither retrieval success, nonzero gradients, matching widths nor unchanged wrapper logits silently become capability claims. For a mathematically prepared beginner using the named warm-up and prerequisite sections, I found the necessary conceptual bridges present and no blocking continuity issue in the assigned path.",
  "checks": {
    "prerequisites": {
      "status": "pass",
      "details": "W.2/W.3 provide data containers, indexing, axes and means before rubrics, boolean bins and RGB tensors; W.5/W.6 provide linear recipes and derivative/update separation before LoRA and vision. Actual7.1/7.3/7.4/7.5 teach roles, assistant-only effective targets, assistant→first-answer prediction and ignored-loss context, which are genuinely reused by8.3 and10.7. Actual1.7/1.8/1.12/1.14/1.15 supply softmax, CE, descent, generation and temperature. Query/Value and FFN/output references in8.8 lead to3.3/3.4 and4.4/4.6. 10.4/10.7 position and causal-mask assumptions lead to4.1 and3.6. New boolean operations, norm/normalization, score axes and false negatives are introduced at their point of use; the11.1 boundary builds directly on10.5/10.6. The forward12.8 example is explicitly a two-class tone task and the9.10 calculations are explained locally, so knowing full audio processing is not an unannounced prerequisite."
    },
    "terminology": {
      "status": "pass",
      "details": "Prompt versus weights, toy target versus sampled model answer, logits versus probability, EOS versus answer correctness, byte tokens versus visible characters, effective target positions versus examples/steps, and sequence indices versus content IDs retain their meanings. 8.7 expressly distinguishes rubric weights from trainable weights. LoRA uses ΔW=(alpha/rank)BA consistently; baseW and bias remain frozen, adapters carry A/B plus settings and base identity, and8.13 does not infer final ΔW from a changed rank alone. 10.3,10.6 and10.7 preserve batch/position/feature axes, and10.9–10.11 specify row=image and column=text before transposition. The classification calibration temperature in9.9/9.10 and pairing temperature in10.10 are distinguished from generation sampling. The projector terminology remains a dimensional interface before a learned semantic bridge at11.1."
    },
    "examples_and_exercises": {
      "status": "pass",
      "details": "Each lesson identifies whether its code prints hand-authored labels, prepares data, computes a gradient, compares representations or performs actual reported training. Exercises keep controlled variables explicit:8.4 removes style coverage;8.5 extraJSON field fails the existing task;8.9 restoring onlyB fails complete adapter identity;9.4 changing onlypermission would leave the stated valid scene;9.7 keeps targetred under changed document interference;9.10 adds paired confidence/truth and derives ECE0.35. In10.2 both patchify/unpatchify sizes change together,10.7 adds image features before a single shift,10.9 swaps candidate columns while retaining float normalization, and10.10 reversed labels deliberately reverse the learning signal. 10.11 changes the objective weighting without changing information. Personally viewed diagrams agree with these transformations. None of these code demonstrations is quietly substituted for generalized model behavior, and actual held-out failures stay visible."
    },
