      "status": "pass",
      "details": "Read the actual original LoRALinear/reliability_bins, ByteTokenizer/render_chat, vision/expansion/wrapper/scene, and TinyLM/loss scopes. LoRA initialization and alpha/rank row-vector computation support8.8/8.13; bytes+8 and assistant targets support8.3; expand_modalities receives unshifted input/labels, insertsignored visual positions and shifts once, supporting10.7. The pure-text wrapper calls the same language model and rejects unmatched placeholders, supporting10.8. The narrative separates the49-question arithmeticcontent base used by8/9 from the45-question directSFT attribute base used by formalprojector/real-modal examples;7.11/7.12 andT.4/T.5 make those different lineages findable. Six-class synthetic vision with new-position holdout is distinguished from fresh Fashion-MNIST branch30/10/10 and officialtest; the separate text-byte mean encoder for contrastive learning loads neither that classifier encoder nor a language model. 9.10 ties its tone numbers to12.8 classifier splits and validation-selected temperature, not safety or whole-response correctness. Actual browser output examples56/True,(1,6,8),ECE0.25 and(1,3,264)/True agree with the read teaching claims. I observed the existing build outputs and did not rerun them or independently reproduce formal training."
